      "text": "I LIVE ---------VERY WILLINGLY, I MIGHT ADD---------ON THE EDGE OF KOREATOWN, LOS ANGELES, CA. , & I DEEPLY RESENT THE WAY LA'S SKID ROW IS PORTRAYED !   1ST, THE CITY HAS SPENT & TODAY STILL SPENDS, BIL;LIONS ON DEALING WITH HOMELESSNESS.  THERE ARE NOW, AS I WRITE THIS, MULTIPLE AGENCIKES & GROUPS DEDICATED TO HELPING PEOPLE   ------PEOPLE--------WHO WANT THE HELP AVAILABLE, TO GET OFF THE STREET.   DAILY , HEALTH CARE PROFESSIONALS RISK LIFE & LIMB TO DELIVER HELP TO THOSE WHO WANT IT .  THE SINGLE BIGGEST PROBLEM IS NOT THE LACK OF HELP OR RESOURCES !  THE #1 PROBLEM IS THAT TOO MANY SIMPLY DO NOT WANT TO BE HELPED & THEY ARE USED TO, & LOVE, THE STREET LIFE !   L.A. GETS MOST OF THESE PEOPLE SIMPLY BECAUSE OF OUR CLIMATE. AND YES, SKID ROW IS A TERRIBLE [PLACE, BUT NOT BECAUSE VOTERS DON'T CARE, & THE CITY OFFICIALS DON'T CARE. EVERY SINGLE PERSON OUT ON THE STREET HAS A REASON ---------A STORY OF WHY THEY ARE THERE, & TOO MANY SIMPLY CANNOT & WILL NOT LEAVE THAT LIFE !  THAT, IS THE HONEST TRUTH.   I'VE BEEN HERE SINCE 1970, & THERE HAS ALWAYS BEEN A SKID ROW ; IT DID HOWEVER, WORSEN EXPONENTIALLY WITH THE 2008 FINANCIAL CRASH.  AND SINCE THEN, THE PROBLEM JUST KEEPS ON WORSENING, DESPITE ALL THE HELP ON EARTH FOR THOSE WHO WISH TO LEAVE THAT LIFE.   THAT, IS THE HONEST TRUTH  OF MY L.A.. -----------------MJL, 80 Y/O",
